Concept: Building a cohort analysis report to calculate "Day 1 Retention"—tracking the exact percentage of newly acquired users who return to a system exactly one day after their first login.
Skills Used: Cohort Analysis, Advanced LEFT JOIN mapping, Window Functions (COUNT() OVER), Date Math (DATE_ADD), Ratio Aggregations.

Engineered a cohort analysis data pipeline to isolate daily user acquisition metrics by extracting first-touch event records from raw activity logs.
Designed strict LEFT JOIN logic binding specific user IDs to chronological calendar intervals, accurately separating genuine retained users from general daily active users (DAU).
Implemented a hybrid SQL architecture utilizing Window Functions to pre-calculate baseline cohort denominators, enabling scalable, precise calculation of Day-1 retention conversion rates.
